<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="fitrana-deep-guide" aria-labelledby="fitrana-deep-heading">
 <h2 id="fitrana-deep-heading">Fitrana calculator and Zakat al-Fitr: complete household guide</h2>
 <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> When you have confirmed the appropriate obligation and your local per-person equivalent, multiply the <strong>number of people you are paying for</strong> by that <strong>verified rate</strong>. The Prophet ﷺ prescribed Zakat al-Fitr as food and instructed it to be given before the Eid prayer in <a href="https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1503" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sahih al-Bukhari 1503</a>. A calculator cannot decide the food measure, cash permissibility or who owes it.</p>
